  "guaranteesTested": [
    "Every live reader acknowledges retirement before the old descriptor backing is retired.",
    "Migration preserves completed work, RNG history, targets, distances, active native contexts and existing task queues.",
    "Two fields share a descriptor owner; migration pauses both at a safe boundary and restores them without restarting.",
    "Temporary write/flush failure or cancellation retains the old authoritative RAM banks and republishes all readers.",
    "Final result publication waits for an overlapping migration.",
    "Queued CPU admission and serialized reclaim expose safe idle boundaries instead of retaining a circular dependency.",
    "Future broker staging is prefunded in the coordinator and kernels; IndexedDB migration completes at 80 MiB.",
    "Actual banks and native heaps appear in the allocation-domain registry without adding policy credits; adopted SAB outputs transfer ownership without double counting.",
    "Automatic storage selection follows current array-buffer pressure and becomes resident again after the recovery token is released."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The experimental dense GPU distance hook, already disabled by default, retains non-revocable descriptor pins to avoid a queued GPU/reclaim cycle; this patch does not change its activation setting.",
    "Native arithmetic and C++ kernels are unchanged. Equality is demonstrated for this finite corpus, not every possible image.",
    "The 80 MiB case admits two concurrent fields with one or two kernels each according to available memory; it does not promise four kernels within that envelope.",
    "Backing retirement and WeakRef collection establish reference eligibility/collection in the test; production runtime does not force garbage collection or claim immediate physical RSS return.",
    "These functional browser runs may overlap other functional tests; their durations are not performance measurements."
  ],
